1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,628
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:06,131
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:10,635
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:16,016
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:19,811
Atoy is Ibyang's real father.

7
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:21,354
You're a fake mother?

8
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:22,689
Something like that, yes.

9
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:28,278
[in English] If you don't want anything
to happen to the woman and child,

10
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:30,864
you will tell me!

11
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:32,866
[in English] Where is the laptop?!

12
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,827
[in English] Do you want to know
where the laptop is?

13
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,662
[Atoy, in English] <i>I need</i>
<i>proof of life first.</i>

14
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:40,081
[grunts]

15
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:41,291
[in English] Who is the mother?

16
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,375
I don't know.

17
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:45,754
The only one who really mattered
to him was Audrey.

18
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:48,006
[Emerson] <i>Oh, then maybe Ibyang</i>
<i>is also Audrey's child.</i>

19
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:50,258
[imitate fighting sounds]

20
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:51,593
- Take it.
- [straining]

21
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:52,510
PREVIOUSLY

22
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:53,970
- [Ibyang] <i>Hello?</i>
- [Atoy on the phone] <i>Ibyang?</i>

23
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:55,722
Ibyang, this is Atoy.

24
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:57,057
Tatoy?!

25
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,224
I-- I-- I was captured.

26
00:00:58,308 --> 00:01:00,310
[Atoy on the phone] <i>Call my boss, Mercado.</i>

27
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:02,020
Call him, tell him where I am.

28
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:04,105
Eh-- Eh, okay, Tatoy.

29
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:05,815
- Just trust, please.
- [sobs]

30
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:07,525
They will save us.

31
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:08,735
[Cita] <i>Atoy is alive?</i>

32
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:10,195
What else did he say?

33
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:13,615
He said he needs help
because he was captured.

34
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:14,699
[gasps]

35
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:16,242
He said he's at--

36
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:17,660
In Bulacan.

37
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:20,497
With Viktor Petrov.

38
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:23,208
[Audrey] <i>So, he's being held</i>
<i>by the ambassador of Zahran!</i>

39
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:27,253
He said we should find his boss, Mercado!

40
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:28,838
As in Jennylyn Mercado?

41
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:30,256
Do you know this man?

42
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:31,966
He often hangs out
at the basketball court.

43
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:33,676
- [man 1] Maybe he's there.
- That's Gavin!

44
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,179
I saw Daddy's men. They're looking for us.

45
00:01:36,262 --> 00:01:38,139
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

46
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:41,851
Karla, hasn't Atoy come home yet?

47
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:44,479
My God, I hope not.

48
00:01:44,562 --> 00:01:45,897
Why, Miss Siony?

49
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:49,692
There's been so much violence here.

50
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:54,489
And isn't there that blond hoodlum
looking for him?

51
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,241
What if…

52
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:58,827
What if he got caught by that guy?

53
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:01,037
[Siony] And then, there's Emerson.

54
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:04,165
Just when they got close,
he got dragged into it.

55
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:06,000
His shop was burned!

56
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:07,418
That's not a coincidence.

57
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:09,087
That's why I'm always ready.

58
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:10,630
I always carry this.

59
00:02:10,713 --> 00:02:13,091
Oh my, Miss Siony,
you've had too much coffee.

60
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:14,467
You're too nervous and alert!

61
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:18,304
But, hey, maybe Miss Siony has a point.

62
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:22,016
Oh, no. That means
Emerson might disappear too.

63
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:25,061
Oh, no! That can't be!
We're not even together yet.

64
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:27,981
You know, Denden, you should court him.

65
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:30,441
Because nothing will happen
if you don't make the move, girl.

66
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:31,359
[Jona] Yes!

67
00:02:31,442 --> 00:02:34,571
[Emerson] Karla, did you see Uno?

68
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:36,156
Do you have his number?

69
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:39,826
Eh, Brother, no, but we met earlier.

70
00:02:39,909 --> 00:02:41,411
I'll just check
if he's at the barbecue stall.

71
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:44,164
If you see him,
tell him to go to Atoy's shop.

72
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:45,456
Tell him it's important.

73
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,292
- I'll update you. All right, brother.
- Yes.

74
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:52,922
Oh. Emerson, Denden has something
to tell you before it's too late.

75
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,008
- [in English] Go.
- Uh…

76
00:02:55,091 --> 00:02:56,885
- Uh…
- [Emerson] Ah.

77
00:02:56,968 --> 00:03:00,430
Uh… It's about… my debt to Brother Kurt!

78
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:02,891
Yes. I'll give it to you instead.

79
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:05,435
But I didn't bring my wallet.

80
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:07,562
Wait, I'll just go back for it, okay?

81
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:08,479
- Okay.
- [indistinct]

82
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:11,566
[Jona] Oh, no.

83
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,568
I know that guy.

84
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:16,487
He looks like the one
who burned down your shop.

85
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,323
[in English] Oh my god, neighbors!

86
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:19,866
The arsonists are here!

87
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:21,576
There they are! There he is!

88
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:23,161
- There! Yes!
- [gasps]

89
00:03:23,244 --> 00:03:24,329
‪[suspicious music playing]

90
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:25,622
Wait.

91
00:03:26,623 --> 00:03:27,624
It's you.

92
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:29,626
You've got some nerve!
You even came back here!

93
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:33,671
Is that all you can do? Here!

94
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:35,215
- [groaning, grunting]
- [squealing]

95
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:36,674
Hey! You're slow, boy!

96
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:38,635
- [grunts and groans]
- [squealing]

97
00:03:38,718 --> 00:03:40,345
[thumping]

98
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:42,931
[screaming and panicking]

99
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:45,141
[clamoring]

100
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,560
Let me borrow your slingshot, boss.

101
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:48,603
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

102
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:49,854
- [grunting]
- [shrieking]

103
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:52,106
[grunting]

104
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:54,234
- [groans]
- [gasps]

105
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:55,610
[Jona] Denden!

106
00:03:55,693 --> 00:03:56,527
‪Come on.

107
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:57,445
‪[squaeling]

108
00:04:00,531 --> 00:04:02,909
[Jona] Denden, stay here, stay here.

109
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:14,170
- [grunting]
- [indistinct]

110
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:20,301
Not me!

111
00:04:20,385 --> 00:04:21,761
‪-[squealing]
‪-[grunting]

112
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:22,971
‪[whimpering]

113
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:27,225
Go ahead!

114
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:29,560
[grunting and groaning]

115
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,982
- [T-Bak] Okay, okay, huh!
- [clamoring]

116
00:04:34,065 --> 00:04:35,316
[Uno] What? Okay, huh?

117
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,901
[clamoring]

118
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,331
[T-Bak] Grab the gun!

119
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,874
Okay! Okay!

120
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:54,419
[music fades]

121
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:56,170
[man] Don't move!

122
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:57,547
‪[suauve theme music playing]

123
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:24,866
[grunts and groans]

124
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:27,368
[grunting and muttering]

125
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:29,370
- [Emerson] What?
- [man] You!

126
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:31,414
Admit it.

127
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:33,082
You kidnapped Atoy, didn't you?!

128
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,876
[Jona] Are you the reason he disappeared?!

129
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:36,294
I don't know what you're talking about!

130
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:38,671
You're a fool, bro. Oh.

131
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:40,757
Better take these guys to the town hall.

132
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:41,841
[Nestor] Yes.

133
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:43,051
[Emerson] These guys
will just cause trouble here.

134
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:44,927
- [Uno] Remember their faces.
- Hey--

135
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,262
Do you know how to speak English?

136
00:05:48,097 --> 00:05:50,141
- Can you speak English?
- Are you okay? Were you hurt? Or…

137
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,351
- Answer!
- [light music laying]

138
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:53,478
I'm fine.

139
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:54,604
You, were you hurt?

140
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:55,646
[Tukmol, in English] You have the right
to remain silent!

141
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:57,940
- [in English] Anything you say can--
- I'm fine.

142
00:05:58,024 --> 00:05:59,901
[Tukmol, in English] Anything
you say can you--

143
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:02,236
Hey, flirt later, huh.

144
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,947
Uno, maybe you can call
your Boss Mercado first.

145
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,324
Atoy needs him now.

146
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,077
Okay, later then, huh.

147
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,079
[indistinct chattering]

148
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:13,247
[light music playing]

149
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:14,832
[music fades]

150
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,417
Okay, okay. Update me.

151
00:06:18,669 --> 00:06:19,587
[Mongki, in English] Boss.

152
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:21,839
What? Did they see Audrey?

153
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,050
[in English] Negative.

154
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,844
Our men saw nothing in Tabang Lupa.

155
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,596
They're still at the precinct now.

156
00:06:28,679 --> 00:06:29,889
Add more men.

157
00:06:29,972 --> 00:06:31,891
Maybe Audrey just slipped past them.

158
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:34,102
I think your sister sensed it.

159
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:36,270
And your son too.
That's why they left that place.

160
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,564
Our boys also said

161
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,399
Atoy is missing.

162
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:42,610
Missing how?

163
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:45,238
Our men are being accused
of kidnapping Atoy.

164
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:46,739
But they don't know anything!

165
00:06:48,157 --> 00:06:50,535
Maybe you ordered someone else, boss.

166
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:53,121
[pensive music playing]

167
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:54,914
I wish we were the ones who kidnapped him.

168
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:58,501
But whoever did it, I hope…

169
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,294
I hope they kill Atoy.

170
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:01,212
[tense music playing]

171
00:07:01,295 --> 00:07:02,672
Less problems for us.

172
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:06,801
[music swells and fades]

173
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:09,262
Brother Jesus.

174
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:12,849
Please bring Tatoy home.

175
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:16,894
Please make him stronger too.

176
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:21,816
Because his voice seemed weak earlier.

177
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:25,278
Send your angels to him.

178
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:30,116
And give him superpowers to help him.

179
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:32,535
Amen.

180
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:34,954
[melancholic music playing]

181
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:05,902
Hey.

182
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:09,780
What are you doing?

183
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:11,699
So, you were just there all this time.

184
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,869
This is for me and Mama.

185
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:22,418
This big dog, she's Mama.

186
00:08:23,002 --> 00:08:25,880
And I'm the puppy.

187
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:28,174
[gentle music playing]

188
00:08:28,257 --> 00:08:30,259
That works…

189
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:31,594
She's just one,

190
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:34,972
but when they're put together again,

191
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:37,850
they're smiling at each other.

192
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:40,603
Let me see.

193
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:43,147
[music fades]

194
00:08:43,814 --> 00:08:44,815
[in English] Corny!

195
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:47,818
[somber music playing]

196
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:49,362
Janine!

197
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:53,032
You're starting to bully me again.

198
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:54,283
Because…

199
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:55,701
Because it looks ugly!

200
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:59,247
I didn't make this to impress you.

201
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:01,332
Janine, you know what a humble pie is?

202
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:04,835
You should eat that, so you'd be humble.

203
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,128
About…

204
00:09:07,296 --> 00:09:08,506
[in English] One hundred slices!

205
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:10,758
[mocking] Whatever. You're still corny!

206
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,219
But I'm serious.

207
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:16,055
Shouldn't you be nice already?

208
00:09:17,056 --> 00:09:21,727
Especially since so many bad things
have happened to your family.

209
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,688
Gosh! What's the connection?

210
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:25,898
You just want to say something!

211
00:09:26,482 --> 00:09:31,654
I mean, our lives can change suddenly.

212
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:34,532
Before, you were free.

213
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:38,536
Now, you have to hide from your Uncle Red.

214
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:40,329
Why would I listen to you?

215
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:42,873
[pensive music playing]

216
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:44,041
And this?

217
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:45,126
This Sister Tonet of yours?

218
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:47,044
She's ugly!

219
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:50,214
There you go again, Janine!

220
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,010
This is Sister Tonet.

221
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:55,928
Do you want her to haunt you?

222
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:59,390
Huh? She made her presence felt before!

223
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:02,310
I don't believe you.

224
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:03,436
Suit yourself!

225
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:19,869
[music fades]

226
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:25,291
[somber music playing]

227
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:34,050
[sneaky music playing]

228
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:46,896
Miss, what did they say?
Will they save Atoy?

229
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:49,190
Yes. He's talking to his boss inside.

230
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:51,609
They said they'll send an extraction team.

231
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:53,110
I'll talk to Boss Mercado first.

232
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:55,946
I need to be on that team
so we can strike back hard for Atoy.

233
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:56,864
Wait, wait.

234
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:58,199
Didn't they send me out

235
00:10:58,282 --> 00:11:00,451
because they had something
confidential to discuss?

236
00:11:00,534 --> 00:11:01,452
Stay here.

237
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:05,748
You know, I think their boss won't allow

238
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:07,458
civilians to be involved.

239
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:09,001
Especially if they're

240
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,711
wimpy, softy.

241
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:12,838
[in English] Wow.

242
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:13,756
[smirks]

243
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:15,424
Wimpy, softy. Me?

244
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,675
[smirks]

245
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:17,802
[in English] Come on.

246
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:19,804
Wow! What do you think I am, a pillow?

247
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:21,180
- Boiled?
- [quirky sting]

248
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:24,100
Even if you slam my head on wood,
the wood will break.

249
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:26,519
What I mean is,

250
00:11:26,602 --> 00:11:29,772
someone without experience in

251
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:31,107
ground combat.

252
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:32,983
I heard about

253
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,693
that Viktor Petrov.

254
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:36,987
The one said to have captured Atoy.

255
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:41,283
Isn't he involved
in a major terrorist group?

256
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:43,994
Oh, so? Do you think you can fight him?

257
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:46,622
[Cita] Mmm, see.

258
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,041
Olga is right.

259
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:53,963
In short, don't meddle
in Uno's and Mercado's plan!

260
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:55,673
They'll just worry about you!

261
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:57,299
- That's harsh, miss.
- Oh?

262
00:11:57,383 --> 00:12:00,302
At least side with me here,
even just a little.

263
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:02,012
You're all so rough on me.

264
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:05,766
You know, if Uno should bring anyone
to their operations…

265
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:07,268
[smirks]

266
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:10,146
…it should be me. Okay?

267
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:13,858
And, also, he wouldn't just
rush in, charge at them,

268
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:16,944
and start shooting just like that, right?

269
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:18,779
Of course, he'd enter cautiously.

270
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:21,740
They'd want to get inside
without anyone noticing.

271
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:25,828
That's how it is! You know, I once worked
as an extra in an indie film.

272
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:27,538
It was exactly like that.

273
00:12:27,621 --> 00:12:29,290
That was the style.

274
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:31,917
But we were in disguise.

275
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:34,879
Oh-- Impressive! You have a point.

276
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:35,838
Right?

277
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:37,840
You should suggest that to Uno, okay?

278
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,049
That would be a big help.

279
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:41,677
Wait, wait, wait. I'll talk to him first.

280
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:44,889
What he needs is a real tough backup.

281
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:47,308
Not extras from a movie, ehem.

282
00:12:47,391 --> 00:12:48,392
[Emerson clears throat]

283
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:49,310
Ugh.

284
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:51,395
- And as a fatter of mact…
- [quirky sting]

285
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:52,605
[both] Huh?

286
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:57,109
Atoy wouldn't be able to do
these missions if I didn't help him.

287
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:58,527
This isn't the first time

288
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,821
I've assisted him
in his dangerous missions, you know?

289
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:02,573
[smirks, in English] And FYI.

290
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:04,492
[in English] For your inconvenience.

291
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:07,995
Atoy's missions wouldn't be successful
without my help.

292
00:13:08,078 --> 00:13:09,038
Hmm, okay!

293
00:13:09,121 --> 00:13:11,123
Yes. He even believes in me
more than I believe in myself.

294
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:13,209
- Okay, fine. That's your story.
- [quirky sting]

295
00:13:13,292 --> 00:13:16,754
But me, I have training in…

296
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:17,963
fighting skills.

297
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:22,301
I can act. I can improvise!

298
00:13:22,384 --> 00:13:26,555
Right? Let's just see who gets chosen
between the two of us, because

299
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,182
it looks like only one will win.

300
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:29,850
[tense music playing]

301
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:32,311
Okay, fine.

302
00:13:34,146 --> 00:13:35,231
But in my heart,

303
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:37,274
you're still the winner.

304
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:39,318
[in English] As always, my love.

305
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:40,236
‪[quirky sting]

306
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:49,453
- [eerie music playing]
- [Ibyang] Janine…

307
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:51,330
What is it?

308
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:56,835
[Ibyang] Janine, wake up.

309
00:13:57,795 --> 00:14:02,174
I'm Sister Tonet.

310
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:04,176
[music swells]

311
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,679
Be good

312
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:08,430
to Ibyang!

313
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,849
- [screams]
- [playful music playing]

314
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:12,393
[in English] Mommy!

315
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:16,689
[Janine, in English] Mommy! Mommy! Mommy!

316
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:18,148
[in English] Mommy, Mommy!

317
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:21,819
- [in English] Mommy! Mommy! [screams]
- Janine. Janine, Janine!

318
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:24,363
- Wake up! Wake up.
- What's happening here?!

319
00:14:24,446 --> 00:14:25,489
[sneaky music playing]

320
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,533
Child, are you okay?

321
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:30,119
- [in English] Mommy, Mommy.
- [in English] What-- What happened?

322
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:32,329
[Ibyang] I don't know.

323
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:34,039
Janine suddenly

324
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:35,583
screamed when I woke up.

325
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:37,960
- [gasping] Huh?
- [whimpering]

326
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:40,754
Mommy, I saw

327
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:43,299
the picture of Sister Tonet
floating in the air.

328
00:14:43,382 --> 00:14:46,135
She's haunting me, Mommy.

329
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:48,304
And she said something to me.

330
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:50,598
[Audrey] Um… [sighs]

331
00:14:50,681 --> 00:14:53,267
Really? Maybe

332
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:55,519
it's because we were talking
about her earlier.

333
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:57,605
What did she say to you?

334
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:01,901
Mommy, just sleep with me.

335
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:04,945
- Child, maybe
- [in English] Please?

336
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:06,488
you were just dreaming?

337
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:09,491
Are you sure you saw a picture
floating in the air?

338
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:10,701
Yes.

339
00:15:10,784 --> 00:15:13,287
I really saw the picture of Sister Tonet.

340
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:16,040
[sneaky music playing]

341
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:24,131
[Ibyang] Janine, whatever
Sister Tonet told you,

342
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:25,466
you should do it.

343
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:31,055
Child, I think you need to drink water.

344
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,307
Let's go downstairs first.

345
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:46,236
[music fades]

346
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:53,285
[knocks on door]

347
00:16:00,292 --> 00:16:01,627
Ibyang.

348
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:05,756
Can I talk to you
before I let Janine in here?

349
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:16,976
[sneaky music playing]

350
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,269
Do you want to tell me something?

351
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,775
Um…

352
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:28,487
- [in English] Good night, sweet dreams.
- [quirky sting]

353
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:32,449
Aside from good night?

354
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:36,620
About what happened to Janine?

355
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:38,706
[music fades]

356
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:41,166
The floating picture?

357
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:43,794
Hmm?

358
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:50,426
You know, I was never close
to your Sister Tonet.

359
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,678
But I think

360
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:55,889
she wouldn't like that you're using her

361
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:57,141
to prank Janine.

362
00:16:58,809 --> 00:17:01,061
Sorry, Aunt Audrey.

363
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:05,274
I'm just annoyed with Janine.

364
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,569
I'm actually nice to her.

365
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:12,823
But she threw away what I made for Mama.

366
00:17:14,616 --> 00:17:17,036
Don't worry. I'll talk to her.

367
00:17:18,203 --> 00:17:19,705
What was it

368
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:21,248
that you made for your mama?

369
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:23,667
Can I see it?

370
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:27,796
[gentle music playing]

371
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,090
[Ibyang] Here.

372
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:32,926
[Audrey] This is so cute.

373
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,261
[chuckles softly]

374
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:36,638
Hmm.

375
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:40,225
Your mother is really lucky to have you.

376
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:45,647
You're truly kind, Ibyang.

377
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:51,695
I'm the lucky one because

378
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:54,782
I've dreamed for so long

379
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:57,659
of finding my mama.

380
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:04,416
[in English] I'm so happy for you, Ibyang.

381
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:10,214
Pray for me, huh.

382
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:12,925
That hopefully…

383
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:17,554
I'll also find what's missing in me.

384
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:21,892
What is it?

385
00:18:27,022 --> 00:18:29,441
Weren't you happy,
even if your child was fake?

386
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:30,901
Your life had purpose.

387
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:33,195
Where is my real child?!

388
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:35,489
[Audrey sobbing]

389
00:18:35,572 --> 00:18:37,157
Who is she?!

390
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:39,284
- [sobs]
- [clicks tongue]

391
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:40,702
[in English] I'll never tell you.

392
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,037
Even if you shoot me.

393
00:18:43,705 --> 00:18:47,918
[melodramatic music playing]

394
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:59,513
Whatever it is you're looking for,

395
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:04,434
I'm sure you'll find it too.

396
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:05,352
[Audrey chuckles]

397
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:08,647
So don't be sad anymore.

398
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:10,774
Smile.

399
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:12,818
[chuckles]

400
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:38,635
[music fades]

401
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:44,933
Miss,

402
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:46,768
please take care of Ibyang.

403
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:49,021
Don't worry about her.

404
00:19:49,104 --> 00:19:51,106
Many people will look after her here.

405
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:53,066
Just come back.

406
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:56,195
There are things you need to face and fix.

407
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,406
I'll handle this.

408
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:07,789
Child, Mama will leave for now.

409
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:09,208
You behave here.

410
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:11,627
[somber music playing]

411
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,086
Please be careful.

412
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:16,506
Bring my Tatoy home.

413
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:25,098
[pensive music playing]

414
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:26,850
When you return,

415
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:30,479
we'll reunite them again,

416
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:35,567
so they'll be happy again.

417
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:41,490
Ibyang.

418
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:44,368
I love you.

419
00:20:46,286 --> 00:20:48,205
Don't forget that, huh.

420
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,291
I love you too.

421
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:57,130
But why are you sad?

422
00:20:57,881 --> 00:20:59,591
- You're crying.
- Oh.

423
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:02,302
No. Oh, no. It's just…

424
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:03,637
[sniffles]

425
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:05,138
[in English] Tears of joy.

426
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:07,557
Um…

427
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:10,227
[inhales]

428
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:12,104
[exhales] Anyway…

429
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:14,523
[melodramatic music playing]

430
00:21:14,606 --> 00:21:16,775
When I return, your life will change.

431
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:21,780
Whoever holds this…

432
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:26,201
will make you happy

433
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:28,954
because that's your family.

434
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:33,625
What do you mean?

435
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:40,173
Just trust me, okay?

436
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:43,427
All right.

437
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,636
I'll go now.

438
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:46,638
Okay.

439
00:21:51,852 --> 00:21:52,936
[sobs]

440
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:58,984
[sentimental music playing]

441
00:22:18,503 --> 00:22:19,588
[sobs]

442
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:28,555
All right. [sniffles]

443
00:22:57,084 --> 00:23:00,212
[music fades]

444
00:23:00,295 --> 00:23:02,005
[traffic humming]

445
00:23:02,589 --> 00:23:04,716
The food here is really good, bro.

446
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:07,469
Ah, yes. But later,
I'll take care of things.

447
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:08,845
The two bottles are on me, hmm!

448
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:11,014
- Really?
- Yes!

449
00:23:11,098 --> 00:23:12,182
- [line rings]
- Okay, I'll cover the bar chow!

450
00:23:12,265 --> 00:23:13,850
- Positive. The two are here.
- Sisig, sisig.

451
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:15,310
Oh, all right, all right.

452
00:23:17,187 --> 00:23:18,897
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

453
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:21,316
- There, just at the corner.
- Great!

454
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:29,116
[footsteps approaching]

455
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:30,283
Oh. What's that?

456
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:32,035
[Uno] Oh?

457
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:34,121
Oh, so? How are you?

458
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:38,750
Are the truck loader's driver
and helper really there?

459
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:41,419
It seems like they're not.

460
00:23:42,003 --> 00:23:44,005
You even took longer.

461
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:47,634
Our intel is reliable,
and I saw them there, eating.

462
00:23:47,717 --> 00:23:49,302
Let's just wait.
Maybe they're not done yet.

463
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:50,762
My God!

464
00:23:50,846 --> 00:23:52,973
They're taking so long to eat!

465
00:23:53,056 --> 00:23:56,059
I've been retouching my makeup
over and over. I'm feeling sticky!

466
00:23:56,143 --> 00:23:57,519
I'm like

467
00:23:57,602 --> 00:24:01,148
a dish in an eatery that's gone cold,
with flies on it.

468
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:03,275
I'm about to rot, almost!

469
00:24:03,358 --> 00:24:04,317
You're unbelievable.

470
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:05,861
So slow.

471
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:08,405
- [sighs]
- Olga, take your position.

472
00:24:08,488 --> 00:24:09,531
- They're here.
- Huh?

473
00:24:10,407 --> 00:24:11,533
They're here.

474
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:13,493
[gasps, mutters]

475
00:24:21,334 --> 00:24:22,460
Huh?

476
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:30,677
[sighs]

477
00:24:31,344 --> 00:24:32,846
[in English] Oh my God!

478
00:24:32,929 --> 00:24:34,097
[in English] My car!

479
00:24:35,223 --> 00:24:37,017
- [in English] Hi, Miss Beautiful!
- Something's smoking!

480
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:38,560
Did your car overheat?

481
00:24:38,643 --> 00:24:39,769
[sighs]

482
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:41,062
Yes.

483
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:43,398
That's easy, ma'am. We'll take care of it.

484
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:44,608
Huh?!

485
00:24:46,109 --> 00:24:47,819
That's embarrassing.

486
00:24:47,903 --> 00:24:51,907
It's okay, brother.
Um, I can just call a mechanic

487
00:24:51,990 --> 00:24:53,658
if I'm bothering you.

488
00:24:53,742 --> 00:24:55,076
It's embarrassing.

489
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:57,120
No, we know how.

490
00:24:57,204 --> 00:24:58,788
- We even have the complete tools.
- Really?

491
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:00,665
They're just in the car truck loader.

492
00:25:01,416 --> 00:25:03,418
Car truck loader? You drive that?

493
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:04,586
- [gasps]
- Yes.

494
00:25:04,669 --> 00:25:07,088
Really?! Wow!

495
00:25:08,298 --> 00:25:09,549
Where is it? Where's--

496
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:10,884
There. It's still parked.

497
00:25:11,551 --> 00:25:14,221
There? Where exactly?

498
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:15,597
- Where?
- At the junkyard!

499
00:25:16,223 --> 00:25:17,599
By the extension.

500
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:19,100
This is easy to fix.

501
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:20,143
Ah, really?

502
00:25:20,227 --> 00:25:21,895
Jaymark, get the tools.

503
00:25:21,978 --> 00:25:23,021
- Ah, okay.
- Okay, ma'am.

504
00:25:23,104 --> 00:25:24,439
Should I open it, brother?

505
00:25:24,522 --> 00:25:25,565
[sneaky music playing]

506
00:25:25,649 --> 00:25:26,608
[in English] Excuse me.

507
00:25:28,735 --> 00:25:31,112
Oh, oops! I dropped it.

508
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:34,407
[thumps, then thuds]

509
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:35,784
Dropped it.

510
00:25:36,451 --> 00:25:37,661
You're peeking, bro.

511
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:39,287
[gasps, grunts]

512
00:25:40,997 --> 00:25:42,707
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

513
00:25:42,791 --> 00:25:43,875
Beautiful, right?

514
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:49,005
Get in!

515
00:25:51,758 --> 00:25:53,593
[music fades]

516
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:55,679
[tense music playing]

517
00:25:55,762 --> 00:25:57,555
[Samir, in English] Let's go! Hurry,
hurry! Pick them up.

518
00:25:57,639 --> 00:25:58,515
[Lily] What are you doing?

519
00:25:58,598 --> 00:25:59,933
Where are you taking us?

520
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:01,142
- [in English] Stand them. Stand them up.
- [Lily] Where are you taking us?

521
00:26:01,226 --> 00:26:02,644
[in English] Let's go. Stand them up.

522
00:26:02,727 --> 00:26:04,145
[gasping]

523
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:05,605
- [both] Stand up.
- [Lily grunts]

524
00:26:05,689 --> 00:26:07,315
[Lily] Where are you taking us?

525
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:10,193
[in English] Didn't I tell you that today
is the day you'll die?

526
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:11,987
[in English] And I'm a man of my word!

527
00:26:12,070 --> 00:26:13,613
[in English] So, prepare to die. Let's go!

528
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:14,531
[in English] What are we waiting for?

529
00:26:14,614 --> 00:26:16,157
- [in English] Bring them. Let's go!
- [Lily] Atoy, what now, Atoy?

530
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:19,202
[Lily sobs] Don't kill us.
Have mercy on us.

531
00:26:19,286 --> 00:26:21,329
[intense music playing]

532
00:26:28,962 --> 00:26:30,338
Oh, sir! Wait!

533
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:33,550
[grunts and groans]

534
00:26:33,633 --> 00:26:35,010
UP NEXT

535
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:37,012
[in English] Gunshots. You two, stay here.

536
00:26:37,512 --> 00:26:39,514
- [grunting]
- [Lily gasps]

537
00:26:39,597 --> 00:26:41,975
[grunting and groaning]

538
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:47,314
- [grunts and groans]
- Help!

539
00:26:48,648 --> 00:26:49,941
That thing is really going to explode!

540
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:52,277
That thing is really going to fire.
[T-bak wails]

541
00:26:52,360 --> 00:26:53,236
[grunts and groans]

542
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:56,614
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

543
00:27:00,368 --> 00:27:02,954
♪ <i>Like a bubble, like a bubble</i> ♪

544
00:27:03,038 --> 00:27:05,457
♪ <i>If the cutter knows where to hit</i> ♪

545
00:27:06,958 --> 00:27:08,335
[music swells]

546
00:27:11,629 --> 00:27:12,797
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

547
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:14,382
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
